# Allowlist, not a denylist. Both Dockerfiles copy exactly the paths
# re-included below, and the compose stack bind-mounts the working tree over
# /app at run time anyway, so nothing else has any business in the build
# context.
#
# The allowlist is what keeps the build working: `projections/` and
# `eventstore/` are bind mounts the service containers own, and Postgres
# creates `projections/pgdata` as uid 70, mode 0700. A denylist would send the
# build context reader in there and fail with "permission denied" the moment
# anyone added a new mount and forgot to list it here.
#
# Adding a COPY to a Dockerfile means adding its path here too.

*

!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!requirements.txt
!requirements/
!src/

# Never ship build artefacts or caches, even from an allowed path.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
src/*/_version.py
